.TH SCAN_XMLESCAPE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
scan_xmlescape \- Scan and decode an XML character entity reference

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/scan.h>
.IB #include <lib/str.h>
.IB #include <lib/uint8.h>

.IB size_t
.IB scan_xmlescape(const char* src, char* dest);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBscan_xmlescape\fR function scans and decodes an XML character entity reference from a given string and stores the result in the location pointed to by \fBdest\fR. The function handles named character entities (e.g., &amp;) and numeric character entities (e.g., &#x3C;).

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB src
The input string containing the XML character entity reference.
.TP
.IB dest
The destination where the decoded character will be stored.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the number of characters processed. If the input string is empty or does not contain a valid character entity reference, the function returns 1 and stores the original character in \fBdest\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBscan_xmlescape\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/scan.h>
#include <lib/str.h>
#include <lib/uint8.h>

int main() {
    const char* input = "&amp;";
    char decoded;
    size_t processed = scan_xmlescape(input, &decoded);
    printf("Decoded character: %c\n", decoded);
    printf("Processed characters: %zu\n", processed);
    return 0;
}
.nef